From: sdarisala <59526515+sdarisala@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:04:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] RCCL: add gfx1250-strict build and device support
 (#12333)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds gfx1250-strict (A0 silicon) as a supported build target for RCCL.

## Motivation

MI450 A0 silicon uses the gfx1250-strict ISA, which is a strict subset
of the gfx1250 (B0) ISA. Previously, RCCL only built device kernels
targeting gfx1250 (B0). To run on A0 hardware, the system relied on
HotSwap — a B0→A0 runtime translation mechanism that caches translated
code objects. This approach introduces a dependency on the translation
cache and is not a sustainable path for production use.

This PR builds native gfx1250-strict RCCL collectives, enabling
distributed-training users to run A0-safe collectives without depending
on HotSwap cached translated objects.

## Technical Details

- Updates DeviceLinker.cmake to recognize and handle gfx1250-strict as a
valid GPU target
- Adds __GFX1250_STRICT__ guards in device kernel primitives
(prims_ll.h, prims_ll128.h, prims_simple.h) to select A0-compatible code
paths
- Updates collective device headers (all_gather.h, all_reduce.h,
broadcast.h, reduce.h, reduce_scatter.h, sendrecv.h) and supporting
headers (device.h, hip_compat.h, rccl_ptr.h, rccl_float8.h) to handle
gfx1250-strict
- Updates generate.py to include gfx1250-strict in kernel generation
- Updates TDM copy path headers for A0 compatibility

## Issue Tracking

JIRA ID: AICOMRCCL-2338

## Test Plan

Setup:
- MI450 machine with GPU A0 revision
- ROCm with gfx1250-strict support:
therock-dist-linux-multiarch-10.2.0.dev0+aa2fc4b65afe4a85221c7e33a1e7dfd10d266bae.tar.gz
- HSA_DISABLE_GFX12_STRICT=0 for gfx1250-strict GPU identification
- RCCL from develop + this PR
- rccl-tests for runtime verification

Test Cases:
(A) Build RCCL explicitly specifying gfx1250-strict as target
(./install.sh --amdgpu_targets "gfx1250-strict") and verify the produced
librccl.so was built for gfx1250-strict.

(B) Build RCCL for local GPU target without explicitly specifying the
target (./install.sh -l) and verify the produced librccl.so was built
for gfx1250-strict.

(C) Build and run rccl-tests against the gfx1250-strict librccl to
verify RCCL kernels are successfully launched and executed on A0
silicon. Verify all 10 collectives pass.

(D) Backward compatibility: unset HSA_DISABLE_GFX12_STRICT and build
RCCL for local GPU target. Verify librccl.so was built for gfx1250.
Build and run rccl-tests against this library. Verify all 10 collectives
pass.

## Test Result

(A) Build successful, completing in the same time as a build without
this patch. Verified librccl.so was built for gfx1250-strict by
inspecting the produced library.

(B) Same as (A).

(C) All 10 collectives passed (all_gather, all_reduce, alltoall,
alltoallv, broadcast, gather, reduce, reduce_scatter, scatter, sendrecv)
with 0 wrong values.

(D) Build successful. Verified librccl.so was built for gfx1250. All 10
collectives passed with 0 wrong values.

